Conclusion:
The analysis indicates that poverty levels in Central Java varied significantly across regencies and cities in 2020. Kebumen, Wonosobo, and Brebes recorded the highest poverty rates, while Semarang City and Salatiga City had the lowest.
The variance value (S² = 132.25) suggests substantial differences in poverty conditions among regions. These findings highlight the importance of equitable economic development and targeted poverty alleviation programs to reduce socioeconomic disparities across Central Java.

